  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "level": "",
    "text": "CONTEXT AND OUTCOME"
  },
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "level": "Heading1",
    "text": "Giving a Voice Assistant a Consistent Character"
  },
  {
    "type": "grid",
    "rows": [
      [
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Context"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Most voice assistants treat every request the same way. Sael explores how voice input, a stable personality prompt, and simple mood cues can make responses feel more continuous and appropriate."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Outcome"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "I built a working Python prototype that listens through the microphone, transcribes speech, routes commands, generates local AI responses, and plays them back as spoken audio."
          }
        ]
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "level": "Heading2",
    "text": "How the System Works"
  },
  {
    "type": "image",
    "file": "image2.png"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "level": "",
    "text": "A complete voice loop with separate input reasoning routing and output modules"
  },
  {
    "type": "grid",
    "rows": [
      [
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "The challenge"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Make voice interaction feel responsive and personal without hiding recognition failures."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "The approach"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Separate listening, command routing, AI generation, and speech output so each part can be tested independently."
          }
        ]
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "level": "",
    "text": "KEY STAGES"
  },
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "level": "Heading1",
    "text": "From Speech to Characterful Response"
  },
  {
    "type": "grid",
    "rows": [
      [
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "1  Listen"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "The microphone captures speech and Google Speech Recognition converts it to text."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "2  Route"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Open and search requests trigger direct computer actions instead of the language model."
          }
        ]
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "grid",
    "rows": [
      [
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "3  Shape tone"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Keyword groups assign tired sad happy angry or default context to the prompt."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "4  Respond"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Ollama runs the OpenHermes model locally and gTTS turns the reply into audio."
          }
        ]
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "grid",
    "rows": [
      [
        [
          {
            "type": "image",
            "file": "image3.png"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Tone routing logic"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "image",
            "file": "image4.png"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Listening and error state"
          }
        ]
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "level": "",
    "text": "FINAL DESIGN AND IMPACT"
  },
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "level": "Heading1",
    "text": "A Small Modular Voice Loop"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "level": "",
    "text": "The prototype exposes its state in the console: listening, recognized speech, recognition failure, and spoken response. This makes the voice loop easy to test while the interaction model is still evolving."
  },
  {
    "type": "image",
    "file": "image5.png"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "level": "",
    "text": "Frame from the 106 second working prototype recording"
  },
  {
    "type": "grid",
    "rows": [
      [
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "5tone states"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "2direct actions"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "106 secrecorded demo"
          }
        ]
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "level": "Heading2",
    "text": "Impact"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "level": "",
    "text": "Sael demonstrates a complete local conversational loop with practical computer actions and visible error handling. Long term memory, relationship continuity, and trained emotion recognition remain research goals rather than finished features."
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "level": "",
    "text": "LEARNING AND NEXT STEPS"
  },
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "level": "Heading1",
    "text": "What the Prototype Taught Me"
  },
  {
    "type": "grid",
    "rows": [
      [
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Learning"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Personality needs consistent rules, but mood keywords alone cannot capture emotional context reliably."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Next step"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "level": "",
            "text": "Add structured conversation memory, test recognition latency, and replace keyword mood routing with a validated classifier."
          }
        ]
      ]
    ]
  }
]
